flow","items":["Sustainability Intern","Sustainability Executive/Analyst","Sustainability Specialist","Sustainability Manager","Senior Sustainability Manager","Head of Sustainability","Sustainability Director","Chief Sustainability Officer"]},{"type":"p","text":"Alternative consulting route:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Sustainability Analyst","ESG Consultant","Senior Consultant","Manager","Senior Manager","Director","Partner"]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong PhD specialisations"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sustainability Science"},{"text":"Climate Science"},{"text":"Environmental Management"},{"text":"Environmental Economics"},{"text":"Climate Policy"},{"text":"Sustainable Development"},{"text":"Circular Economy"},{"text":"Sustainable Supply Chains"},{"text":"Renewable Energy Systems"},{"text":"Climate Risk"},{"text":"Environmental Engineering"},{"text":"Resource Management"},{"text":"Sustainable Finance"},{"text":"Urban Sustainability"},{"text":"Environmental Policy"},{"text":"Industrial Ecology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"2040–2046"},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest senior professionals will move beyond compliance reporting into business transformation. A future Sustainability Director should be able to connect carbon reduction, resource efficiency, supply-chain resilience, climate risk, sustainable finance and business growth rather than treating sustainability as only an environmental-reporting function."}]}]}